        "content": "### Pitch\n\nInstructor PHP helps insurance technology teams turn unstructured documents and customer communications into validated, typed data—then use that data in provider-flexible AI workflows built for existing PHP systems. Apply it to claims intake, underwriting, policy servicing, and knowledge retrieval, with validation, retry controls, bounded evidence context, and observable agent workflows.\n\n### Insurance problems it can help solve\n\n- **Claims intake:** Extract loss details, dates, parties, and requested actions from FNOL narratives, emails, and supporting documents.\n- **Underwriting triage:** Structure submission information and flag missing fields for human review.\n- **Policy servicing:** Classify and route requests such as address changes, coverage questions, and cancellations.\n- **Claims knowledge retrieval:** Find relevant policy wording and claims guidance, with bounded evidence context to support an answer.\n- **Operational automation:** Coordinate repetitive workflows with configurable tools and stop conditions, while keeping humans in the review loop.\n- **Technology flexibility:** Integrate through PHP and switch among supported LLM providers without rewriting application-level inference code.",
